Two consequences are easy to misread, so they are stated here:

  - The source is readable in this repository, and resourceExposurePolicy in app/app.json
    permits debugging and downloading the source from a tenant where the app is installed.
    Neither is a grant of rights. Both exist so a customer can support and audit what runs
    in their own environment.

  - This repository does not build on its own. It requires the private bc-dev-templates
    repository, which is separately licensed and not covered by this file.

Third-party components remain under their own licences. Microsoft Dynamics 365 Business
Central, the AL language, and the Microsoft base and system applications are Microsoft's,
and nothing here grants any right in them.

For any use beyond the end-user licence agreement, contact the publisher through the URL
in app/app.json.
